    {
      "id": 7429716486073125,
      "plugin": "StochasticTelegraph",
      "model": "Fermata",
      "version": "2.0.30",
      "params": [],
      "rightModuleId": 5694575490455203,
      "data": {
        "text": "REMODULON\n=========\n\nTwo MINISTEPS run off triggers passing through MULT. Set their period lengths independently in the \"MAX\" field if you want. Prime ratios of step length to \"MAX\" evoke intrigue and romance - and if \"MAX\" is prime, every step length is relatively prime. Higher modulo values are more conducive to chaotic perturbation.\n\nStep length is controlled by a CVMIX whose three attenuverters balance:\n\n1. Static voltage, unless you plug something in\n2. Feedback from this MINISTEP\n3. Cross-feedback from other MINISTEP.\n\nSequences grow less periodic with more feedback, and cross-feedback between the oscillators can bring you to some very strange places indeed.\n\nBut wait there's more. We'll also send you an LLFO to drive the thing with, plus a chest of useful tools - from a simple crossfade and lightweight comparator to a highly flexible clock divider and even FEIGEN which does the same thing as REMODULON sort of except different and cooler. Find them in the nearby selection <friends of remodulon.vcvs>.",
        "width": 3,
        "screen_colors": 45848490672128,
        "font_choice": "fonts/RobotoMono-Bold.ttf",
        "visible_lines": 28,
        "title_text": "REMODULON"
      },
      "pos": [
        102,
        2
      ]
    },
