    {
      "id": 6852482002269709,
      "plugin": "StochasticTelegraph",
      "model": "Fermata",
      "version": "2.0.30",
      "params": [],
      "rightModuleId": 4318405816629772,
      "data": {
        "text": "FRIENDS OF REMODULON\n====================\n\nTools I find useful to apply to REMODULON.\n\nLLFO\nMy preferred source of gates. Simple and controllable.\n\nXFADE\nCombine different sequences, on different clocks, in different conceptual gestalts, thesis and counterthesis.\n\nVCA\nRing-modulating two patterns together can produce novel results, more lively than a crossfade but less flexible\n\nCOMPARATOR\nAn information reducer turning complex signals into complex binary rhythms. All outputs useful. A narrow-band \"A=B\" detection can produce rhythms that reward fine-tuning and patience.\n\nRKD\nA clock divider. Paired with a S&H (included) it convolutes cyclic patterns and can reveal hidden recurrences in more complex ones\n\nFEIGEN\nAn honest to goodness model of Edward Lorenz's logistic map equation. \"GROWTH\" is analogous to REMODULON's same-channel feedback control. Outputs from high values are properly formally chaotic. The function it uses has a term in it REMODULON's does not, it bifurcates, look it up, there's a great wikipedia. Run it off the same clock and use the rest of these tools to compare it to a REMODULON, or you know do whatever",
        "width": 3,
        "screen_colors": 45848490672128,
        "font_choice": "fonts/RobotoMono-Bold.ttf",
        "visible_lines": 28,
        "title_text": "friends of remodulon"
      },
      "pos": [
        128,
        2
      ]
    },
